WEBVTT

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:05.700
Taka-kun, I left early 
again today, okay? -Charles

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:07.120
<i>Today we're broadcasting from Hatsune Island, 
home of the Everlasting Cherry Blossom Tree.</i>

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:08.700
<i>Fuji-san, if you will.</i>

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:12.700
<i>Yes, we're here live from Hatsune Island.</i>

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:23.820
Nii-san.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:25.610
Good morning.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:27.530
Yeah, good morning.

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:31.500
<b>Da Capo</b>

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:36.500
It's still cold outside, isn't it?

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:37.500
Yeah.

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:39.710
With the cherry blossoms 
always in bloom like this,

00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:41.940
you can't tell when spring 
is coming, can you?

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:43.150
Not at all.

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:48.950
It's so cute!

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:55.490
If we don’t hurry, we'll miss the bus.

00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:57.690
Oh... Later, then.

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:59.720
Nii-san, wait!

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:11.430
Good morning, Senpai, Katsuragi-san.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:13.040
Good morning!

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:14.890
Good morning.

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:15.520
Good morning.

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:26.740
It's almost time for the 
graduation ceremony, isn't it?

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:29.450
The days go by quick, don't they?

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:32.160
Speaking of graduation, 
there's the party.

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:36.200
It seems like Lulu-nee's been busy 
preparing for that recently.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:39.330
What are going to do about our 
graduation edition of the newspaper?

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.520
I heard about Sakura-chan 
later from Ricca-san...

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:48.870
Continuing to investigate the Everlasting 
Cherry Blossom Tree would be...

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:52.380
Why don't we just leave her be?

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:56.880
I agree with you.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:57.800
Me, too.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:03:58.830
Yes!

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:05.990
I wonder what's going 
to happen this evening.

00:04:04.190 --> 00:04:05.990
Tomorrow evening, come to the 
Everlasting Cherry Blossom Tree...

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:07.560
I'm excited.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:10.420
Speaking of which, 
we never did solve the mystery

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:11.760
of that message we received before.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:15.070
The one that said, 
"When the cherry blossoms bloom,

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:16.600
go to the promised place"?

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:18.600
I think both those mysterious messages

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:21.910
must have something to do 
with each other, but...

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:23.910
Nii-san, what do you think?

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:27.100
I'm not sure...

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:29.940
But I think, once we figure 
out yesterday's message,

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:33.120
we'll be able to unravel the mystery 
behind the one we received before.

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:37.090
In other words, everything will 
become clear this evening, right?

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:41.010
Well, it's nothing more than intuition, though...

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:43.570
You might be right, Kiyotaka.

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:45.020
Ricca-san!

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:46.910
Good morning!

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:49.630
Actually, about the graduation edition...

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:53.040
We were all just talking about that.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:53.870
And?

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:57.170
Keeping Sakura in mind, 
we decided it would be

00:04:57.170 --> 00:05:00.140
better to write our articles 
from a different angle.

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:01.950
I think so, too.

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:02.980
Ricca-san...

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:09.770
Is it just me, or are those 
two acting suspicious?

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:10.390
Huh?

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:12.160
Ever since the events with Sakura-chan,

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:15.300
it feels like those two have 
suddenly grown a lot closer...

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:17.560
I think so, too.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:24.300
Self study

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:37.650
Student Council Room

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:41.790
If anyone has any opinions regarding 
this year's graduation party...

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:42.690
I do!

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:43.960
Ricca?

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:45.920
You're very motivated today.

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:48.090
My, my, how unusual.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:49.530
Go ahead, Ricca.

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:50.870
Yes.

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:54.720
I see you're back to normal.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:55.370
Huh?

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:58.300
Lately you've been looking down, 
and I was worried about you.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:03.230
After I learned about Sakura-chan, 
I thought, "Oh, so that's why," but...

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:05.870
Have I been acting that strange lately?

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:07.010
Strange?

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:11.680
I'd say you've always been strange, actually...

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:12.980
What do you mean?

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:14.520
Now, now.

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:19.560
Still, we're about to graduate soon ourselves,
 but it just doesn't feel that way...

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:20.990
You're right...

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:25.560
Though, there is one thing I have to 
make clear before our graduation.

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:26.330
Huh?

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:39.040
So then Tony...

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:39.040
Yoohoo!

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:40.850
Taka-kun!

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:44.040
Hey, Lulu-nee!

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:45.920
It's just our usual skinship.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:49.090
I asked you to hold back at school....

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:50.920
Then, it's okay if we're at home?

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:53.950
Where at home? The living room? In bed?

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:56.430
Or... in the bathroom?

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:58.160
Th-That's not what I mean...

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:00.570
You don't like it?

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:04.400
It's not that I don't like it, just...

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:05.080
Nii-san!

00:07:08.350 --> 00:07:09.270
Himeno?

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:13.200
Forget it!

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.820
Hey, Himeno!

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:20.570
Senpai?

00:07:20.570 --> 00:07:21.290
Sara...

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:22.720
Did something happen?

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:25.440
Well... nothing, really.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:28.240
What about you, Sara? Did you need me?

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:31.210
Oh, yes... No, well...

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:35.970
Senpai, could you help me practice 
my swings after school?

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:37.140
Your swings?

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:38.490
For softball...

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:41.000
Do you mind?

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:43.550
I'd love to help you practice,

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:45.410
but after school we're all 
going to check that message...

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:47.210
Oh, that's right!

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:48.610
Maybe next time.

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:50.100
Yes.

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:53.930
What's wrong? You seem off today, Sara.

00:07:53.930 --> 00:07:56.290
Huh?! D-Do I?

00:07:56.290 --> 00:07:57.590
Kiyotaka-san!

00:07:57.590 --> 00:07:58.630
Aoi-chan?

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:03.330
It's sad to see Sakura-chan gone, isn't it?

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:06.260
Y-Yeah, I guess... But...

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:10.580
Um, please let me know whenever 
you're feeling sad, okay?

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:15.050
If you'd like, I'll treat you 
to my naked apron anytime.

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:16.240
No, that's...

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:18.040
Naked... apron?

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:19.510
Ah! Sara?!

00:08:19.510 --> 00:08:20.510
How dirty!

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:22.500
It's not, um...

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:26.600
I'm waiting in the courtyard. -Himeno

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:26.180
Himeno?

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:33.380
Himeno.

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:34.960
Nii-san.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:37.920
Sorry about earlier. I kind of, um...

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:39.410
It doesn't matter anymore.

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:42.970
I see... By the way, 
what did you need me for?

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:46.140
What's wrong?

00:08:47.390 --> 00:08:48.810
Don't stare at me.

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:51.210
Oh, sorry.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:56.830
Himeno.

00:08:58.070 --> 00:08:59.350
Tell me.

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:02.220
Tell me how you feel, Nii-san.

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:03.220
How I feel?

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.510
Nii-san, who do you—

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:11.900
Taka-kun! There you are!

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:15.690
Caught you!

00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:16.900
Lulu-nee, again?

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:20.000
Taka-kun, your feelings are for me, right?

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:22.070
Jeez, Charles-san!

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:24.680
Charles-san, you're not being fair!

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:25.860
H-Hey...

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:28.650
Jeez, everyone, what are you doing?!

00:09:28.650 --> 00:09:29.830
How dirty!

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:33.770
Hey!

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:34.590
Kousuke?

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:36.890
You look like you're worn out.

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:38.080
Not really...

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:41.690
Now, is it because you were suddenly 
hugged by Charles-senpai in the hallway?

00:09:42.730 --> 00:09:44.700
And then afterwards invited to 
practice swings with Sara-chan,

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:46.020
followed by a temptation from Aoi-chan,

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:47.570
and now this scene in the 
courtyard with Himeno-chan?!

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:49.230
Are you some stalker?

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:51.070
There it is! That sigh!

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:53.740
You're wondering which girl 
you should choose, aren't you?

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:58.100
Must be nice, being able to worry 
about something like that.

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:01.650
I really envy a happy celebrity like you.

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:03.970
I envy you...

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:10.860
So this is where you've been.

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:12.520
Ricca-san...

00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:15.060
Sheesh, I spent a while searching for you.

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:16.670
Did you need me?

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:17.460
Yes.

00:10:17.690 --> 00:10:19.660
I forgot to give you this at lunch.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:25.810
It's still a bit too cold to eat on the roof.

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:31.310
Don't complain.
 This'll help you stay warm, right?

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:33.480
Well... But...

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:36.120
If anybody saw us like this...

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:38.220
I don't really mind, but...

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:40.120
Do you?

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:41.220
I...

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:42.810
There's no way you would, right?

00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:46.620
The two of us have already kissed, so...

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:49.530
Huh? Ah... R-Ricca-san!

00:10:53.140 --> 00:10:55.730
Ricca-san, can I ask you a question?

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:56.470
What?

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:58.830
It's about Sakura...

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:00.340
About Sakura?

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:03.680
Uh... I can't say this very well, but...

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:07.910
For some reason... I get a feeling 
we'll be able to see Sakura again.

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:09.250
So?

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:11.580
Ricca-san, do you know anything?

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:15.150
Um, in the memories of
 your past life, or anything...

00:11:15.620 --> 00:11:18.790
Why do you think that's 
related to my past life?

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:24.670
Because, well... you remembered 
more when you met Sakura...

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:29.930
So I thought she might have 
something to do with your past...

00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:36.270
Besides, it seems like you might know 
something I don't about Sakura...

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:38.840
Do you want to hear about our past life?

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:39.800
Yes.

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:42.980
Then where should I start...

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:51.060
After all, I was a category 5 mage,
 known as The Lone Cattleya.

00:11:52.530 --> 00:11:55.430
I remembered all kinds of interesting tales,

00:11:55.430 --> 00:11:57.750
like using magic to solve cases.

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:00.500
No, not those stories...

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:01.900
I know!

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:07.170
You're talking about the night 
we first became one, right?

00:12:08.780 --> 00:12:12.510
You were so manly that night!

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:15.570
I don't meant those stories either...

00:12:15.980 --> 00:12:17.600
Jeez, Ricca-san...

00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:21.150
What do you want to know that for?

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:29.230
It's been a while, Yoshino Kiyotaka!

00:12:29.230 --> 00:12:30.790
Huh? How?!

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:34.790
Lately it seems you all have been 
too involved with this girl Sakura,

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:37.800
causing you to neglect your newspaper!

00:12:38.710 --> 00:12:41.370
We don't need you worrying about us!

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:42.540
Have you forgotten?!

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:44.730
Our competition is not over yet!

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:45.710
It's not!

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:50.280
Seriously, don't forget it!

00:12:50.650 --> 00:12:53.430
Your competition doesn't even matter.

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:55.340
Let's go, Kiyotaka.

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:56.550
Uh, right.

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:59.290
Wait! We will not allow such selfish action!

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:03.220
Taka-kun, I found you!

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:05.150
We were all looking for you!

00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:06.200
Yes!

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:10.030
Just when I wondered who you were with...

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:14.830
That's not fair, Ricca! 
Hogging Taka-kun!

00:13:15.130 --> 00:13:15.940
Huh?

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:18.530
I've been holding back so far,

00:13:18.530 --> 00:13:22.550
but Taka-kun, just who do 
you have feelings for?

00:13:22.550 --> 00:13:24.330
Huh? Again?

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:27.120
I'm asking you which girl 
you choose, Taka-kun!

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:27.870
Huh?

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:30.560
That certainly would be a good 
thing to make clear, wouldn't it?

00:13:30.560 --> 00:13:31.960
Even you, Ricca-san?

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:33.990
Nii-san, this is a good opportunity.

00:13:33.990 --> 00:13:35.060
That's right.

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:37.460
Today, we're going to 
have you make it clear.

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:39.630
So, who do you choose?

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:42.300
Huh? But that's...

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:48.860
Um... Suginami-sama, I think we're 
being completely neglected here...

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:50.910
Club Member #1!

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:51.730
Yes!

00:13:56.220 --> 00:13:57.940
They got us good.

00:13:57.940 --> 00:13:59.880
What was that, just now?

00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:00.920
I don’t know.

00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:03.690
Huh? Where's Taka-kun?

00:14:07.350 --> 00:14:09.510
We should be all right this far away.

00:14:09.510 --> 00:14:10.250
Yes.

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:21.380
Um, continuing our earlier discussion...

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:24.640
Are Sakura and your past...

00:14:24.640 --> 00:14:25.940
More importantly!

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:27.810
Who do you choose, Kiyotaka?

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:31.100
You're still on that?

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:33.280
Well, it's important!

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:37.210
The past isn't important!

00:14:38.470 --> 00:14:41.950
What I remembered, 
what happened in the past,

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:44.520
frankly, none of that matters.

00:14:45.060 --> 00:14:50.470
But... If you're the only one who knows, 
it doesn't feel fair.

00:14:50.680 --> 00:14:51.800
Not fair?

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:53.560
I guess...

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:55.990
But you knowing that doesn't mean

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:58.480
it's going to turn out that way in the future.

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:01.890
Besides, that wouldn't be 
much fun, would it?

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:04.820
Just moving along a path 
to predetermined results.

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:06.720
Ricca-san...

00:15:07.060 --> 00:15:09.190
So what's important is the present.

00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:12.630
Sakura made her decision and moved on.

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:16.270
It's about time we made 
our own decisions, too.

00:15:16.840 --> 00:15:17.960
You're right.

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:19.100
So!

00:15:19.950 --> 00:15:26.000
What's important is how you 
currently feel about me, right?

00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:28.570
But... That has nothing to do with...

00:15:29.140 --> 00:15:31.010
My feelings haven't changed.

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:32.680
Just like I told you before,

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:37.620
I love you now, as my present self.

00:15:39.150 --> 00:15:41.280
So, what about you?

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:43.290
Ricca-san...

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:45.180
Hey, Kiyotaka...

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:47.530
Let's kiss.

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:53.220
You said so before... next time, 
you wanted me to ask first...

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:56.200
Yes, I did say that, but...

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:07.860
Ahh, this is the same as last time...

00:16:08.310 --> 00:16:10.540
Next time I want you to ask me, Kiyotaka.

00:16:10.920 --> 00:16:11.830
Ricca-san...

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:13.790
There he is!

00:16:14.310 --> 00:16:16.870
Jeez, we were looking for you!

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:18.510
Oh, sorry, sorry...

00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:20.300
Now we're all here.

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:22.920
So, let's continue!

00:16:24.030 --> 00:16:28.490
Nii-san, this is very important to all of us.

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:31.540
B-But...

00:16:31.940 --> 00:16:33.390
Then let's ask once again.

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:35.860
Kiyotaka, who do you choose?

00:16:36.840 --> 00:16:39.900
Well, um, you see... I...

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:42.910
I...

00:16:45.220 --> 00:16:47.360
wish we could stay like this forever...

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:49.370
What?

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:51.960
Did I say something wrong?

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:55.530
Sheesh, that's not answering the question!

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:58.000
Now I feel stupid for being nervous.

00:16:58.230 --> 00:16:59.360
You said it.

00:16:59.670 --> 00:17:03.270
Well, this indecisiveness is 
just like Kiyotaka, though.

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:06.440
Honestly, it really is just like Nii-san...

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:45.850
Good evening. It's been a while.

00:17:46.760 --> 00:17:50.850
Or should I say, nice to meet you?

00:17:53.070 --> 00:17:54.650
Sakura-chan?

00:17:55.030 --> 00:17:57.800
But... she doesn't seem the same...

00:17:57.800 --> 00:18:00.660
Plus, she said nice to meet you...

00:18:04.690 --> 00:18:05.660
Who are you?

00:18:06.470 --> 00:18:09.370
I'm... Yoshino Sakura.

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:12.470
What do you mean?

00:18:12.470 --> 00:18:13.770
That's right,

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:16.110
you all helped take care of 
the other me, didn't you?

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:17.990
The other you?

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:24.340
All of us have met before 
in a different place.

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:28.920
Judging from your reactions, 
it looks like none of you remember...

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:30.820
Don't remember?

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:38.360
What I know is the fun times that 
I spent together with all of you...

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:45.310
And the final promise we all 
made in the very end.

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:51.040
When the cherry blossoms bloom, 
go to the promised place...

00:18:51.300 --> 00:18:53.480
Then, you sent that message?!

00:18:53.720 --> 00:18:54.480
Yes.

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:59.630
It took a bit of time, but I was 
finally able to see you all again...

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:04.060
Wh-What's going on?

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:06.200
This all feels kind of nostalgic.

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:09.610
I've been thinking that same thing...

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:13.880
I don't understand why, 
but it feels very nostalgic...

00:19:16.010 --> 00:19:19.370
That's because you're the one 
I was most attached to, Kiyotaka.

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:20.900
What?! Really?!

00:19:20.900 --> 00:19:24.840
Wow, Kiyotaka is as popular as ever.

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:28.510
A-Anyway, you know something, don't you?

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:33.080
Everyone, will you listen to my story?

00:19:34.750 --> 00:19:37.980
It's a bit of a long story,

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:41.490
but once you hear it, 
I think everything will be solved.

00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:45.210
See, I even have the perfect snacks.

00:19:45.930 --> 00:19:47.370
W-Wow!

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:48.770
Sleight of hand?!

00:19:49.050 --> 00:19:51.170
No, it's magic.

00:19:51.430 --> 00:19:52.340
Magic...

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:56.370
This is all I can do now, though.

00:19:56.370 --> 00:19:57.240
But...

00:19:57.610 --> 00:19:59.680
this is one of the best magic spells

00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:02.250
for making people smile.

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:11.700
Now then, are you ready to listen?

00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:15.130
One girl, and one cherry blossom tree.

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:18.260
One promise and one modest wish...

00:20:19.040 --> 00:20:25.180
And a precious feeling that remained 
unchanged for decades, even centuries.

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:28.540
No matter how many 
seasons came to pass,

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:34.020
spring would always come, 
carrying the smell of fresh cherry blossoms.

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:40.640
A tale of beginnings, 
and that dream-like dream,

00:20:41.240 --> 00:20:45.420
repeating just like a da capo.

00:22:28.900 --> 00:22:30.660
Hello, young lady.

00:22:36.060 --> 00:22:37.220
What's wrong?

00:22:40.390 --> 00:22:42.010
Are you... asking me?

00:22:42.290 --> 00:22:43.060
Yes.

00:22:48.260 --> 00:22:49.250
What's wrong?

00:22:49.680 --> 00:22:50.910
Um...

00:22:53.600 --> 00:22:55.310
That's a very pretty light pink.

00:22:56.040 --> 00:22:58.760
It's very cute, just like you.

00:22:59.160 --> 00:22:59.920
Huh?

00:22:59.920 --> 00:23:01.170
I'm talking about that.

00:23:03.760 --> 00:23:06.360
You... know what this is?

00:23:07.060 --> 00:23:08.530
It's a "sakura," isn't it?

00:23:08.530 --> 00:23:11.490
Yes, though I've never 
seen that variety before.

00:23:12.160 --> 00:23:13.990
Saku...ra?
